{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Eightfold.OctonionicSu3RankObstruction","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Eightfold.OctonionicSu3RankObstruction","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.Constructions","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.Finrank","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.FiniteDimensional.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.LinearIndependent.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.LinearIndependent.Lemmas"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.no_faithful_generator_identification","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.no_faithful_generator_identification","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OctonionicSu3RankObstruction.lean#L118-L130","doc":"**The concrete dimension count.** `su(3)` has dimension 8 as a real Lie\nalgebra and `Im(𝕆)` has dimension 7, so no identification of the eight Gell-Mann\ngenerators with the seven imaginary units is faithful.\n\nStated over a generic division ring rather than `ℝ`, per the base-ring\nconvention: nothing archimedean is used, and the count is what does the work.\nThe hypothesis is not decoration — swap the two dimensions and the statement is\nfalse, since `K⁷ → K⁸` admits plenty of injections. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.cartan_not_independent_on_one_unit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.cartan_not_independent_on_one_unit","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OctonionicSu3RankObstruction.lean#L107-L114","doc":"The rank obstruction, stated for the two Cartan generators by name: whenever\nboth are carried onto the same imaginary unit `u`, they are dependent, and the\nrank-2 Cartan of `su(3)` has collapsed to a line. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.not_linearIndependent_of_common_line","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.not_linearIndependent_of_common_line","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OctonionicSu3RankObstruction.lean#L86-L105","doc":"**The rank obstruction.** Two vectors that are multiples of a common vector\nare linearly dependent — with no side condition on the multipliers at all.\n\nThis is the collapse of a rank-2 Cartan onto a single imaginary unit: if `I₃` and\nthe hypercharge `Y` are both sent to multiples of `e₃`, they cannot be\nindependent, whatever the multipliers are.\n\nNo nonvanishing hypothesis is needed. The obvious relation `b·(a • x) − a·(b • x)`\nis nontrivial only when `a` or `b` is nonzero, but the degenerate case is not an\nexception: if both vanish the pair is `(0, 0)`, and a family containing `0` is\nnever independent either. Stating it without the hypothesis is therefore both\nstronger and closer to the fact being used. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Eightfold.no_injective_of_finrank_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Eightfold.no_injective_of_finrank_lt","kind":"theorem","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Eightfold/OctonionicSu3RankObstruction.lean#L71-L78","doc":"**The dimension obstruction.** A linear map into a space of strictly smaller\nfinite dimension is never injective.\n\nApplied below with `V = su(3)` (dimension 8) and `W = Im(𝕆)` (dimension 7). ","signatureChunk":0}]}